[A10] OWNER DECISION (2026-11-27 12:41) on item 5 of the round-10c ruling (comment 7216582862): THE TRANSMIT's stated row at 8x8/1if goes from 77 to **80 ms**, the cap named in `ctrl_loop.h`'s header. Every other bound is unchanged:
- load: 0.70 at 1x1/1if, 0.77 at 8x8/1if;
- last notice: 140 ms;
- ACMP: 30 ms;
- txL: 49 ms;
- THE SHARE: 2 ms.

The hold-off stays at 8 cs, so no image byte moves (round 10d proves this with an identity build). Round 10d keeps that commit.
